{
  "configuration_id": "config_011",
  "reason": "With no prior experiments, the most critical uncertainty is establishing a strong single-modality baseline to judge whether multimodal fusion, multiprofile aggregation, or more complex encoders actually add value. config_011 (rna_only, singleprofile, scvi_n200) provides a clean, well-established reference: scVI is a standard learned encoder in single-cell genomics, singleprofile avoids confounding from aggregation strategy, and the RNA-only setting isolates the contribution of gene expression without image modality. This baseline lets every subsequent multimodal or multiprofile experiment be interpreted as a delta over a meaningful (not trivially weak) starting point. It is the highest-information first experiment because it anchors the comparison space for modality, profile, and encoder choices simultaneously without introducing multiple untested complexities at once."
}

